    old "Laying there, she slowly felt her senses come back to her."
    new "Acostada allí, sintió lentamente que sus sentidos volvían a ella."

    old "When she opened her eyes again, he was laying there next to her."
    new "Cuando abrió los ojos de nuevo, él yacía allí a su lado."

    old "His arms, broad as logs, wrapped around her body."
    new "Sus brazos, anchos como troncos, envolvieron su cuerpo."

    old "As the pace of her heart slowed, she nestled herself into his arms, resting her head on his broad chest."
    new "A medida que el ritmo de su corazón se calmaba, ella se acomodó en sus brazos, apoyando la cabeza sobre su amplio pecho."

    old "And just as how submitting came natural to her with him, so too did the safety."
    new "Y así como la sumisión le resultaba natural a ella con él, también lo era la seguridad."

    old "The safety she only felt in his arms."
    new "La seguridad que solo sentía en sus brazos."

    old "How he held her tight, and how his brutal ways softened with her, stroking the surface of her skin with gentle touch."
    new "Cómo la abrazaba con fuerza, y cómo sus brutales maneras se suavizaban con ella, acariciando la superficie de su piel con un toque delicado."

    old "Forever, it seemed, they laid there by the fire together."
    new "Para siempre, parecían yacer allí junto al fuego."

    old "Only when the fire faded did he move."
    new "Solo cuando la hoguera se apagó, él se movió."

    old "I must go now."
    new "Debo irme ahora."

    old "Stay longer."
    new "Quédate más tiempo."

    old "I will set up in camp, but I promise I will be back soon."
    new "Me estableceré en el campamento, pero prometo que volveré pronto."

    old "Sarah sighed, upset at having to keep up appearances, even as she knew it was wisest."
    new "Sarah suspiró, molesta por tener que mantener las apariencias, aunque sabía que era lo más sensato."

    old "Don't leave for another five years though."
    new "No te vayas por otros cinco años."

    old "He softly laughed."
    new "Rió suavemente."

    old "Never again."
    new "Jamás más."

    old "Sarah watched Atilla get dressed, sad to see the armor cover up his body."
    new "Sarah observó a Atilla vestirse, triste de ver cómo la armadura cubría su cuerpo."

    old "Before he left, he turned to her."
    new "Antes de irse, se volvió hacia ella."

    old "Before I forget, the message."
    new "Antes de olvidarlo, el mensaje."

    old "He casually tossed a letter onto her desk."
    new "Sin pensarlo, él arrojó una carta sobre su escritorio."

    old "The letter. War. Threats. The real world."
    new "La carta. La guerra. Amenazas. El mundo real."

    old "This...this had been but a brief intermission, she thought with sad heart."
    new "Esto... esto había sido solo un breve intermedio, pensó con el corazón triste."

    old "Yes, Sarah?"
    new "¿Sí, Sarah?"

    old "He looked at her as he stood in the entrance of the tent."
    new "La miró mientras se paraba en la entrada de la tienda."

    old "You said you'd marry me."
    new "Dijiste que te casarías conmigo."

    old "Yes."
    new "Sí."

    old "His voice was solemn. He had meant every word of it."
    new "Su voz era solemne. Había significado cada palabra."

    old "Can I ask for a gift?"
    new "¿Puedo pedir un regalo?"

    old "Of course. A wife has a right."
    new "Por supuesto. Una esposa tiene derecho."

    old "What do you want?"
    new "¿Qué quieres?"

    old "Sarah looked at his mighty frame. His warrior's build."
    new "Sarah observó su imponente estructura. La constitución de un guerrero."

    old "I would like the same gift you gave me today."
    new "Me gustaría el mismo regalo que me diste hoy."

    old "But a thousand more."
    new "Pero mil más."

    old "Atilla grinned, flashing his sharp teeth."
    new "Atilla sonrió, mostrando sus dientes afilados."

    old "I will build a mountain from their heads. Offer up their gutted hearts."
    new "Construiré una montaña con sus cabezas. Ofrezco sus corazones arrancados."

    old "The rivers of Rosanna will turn crimson as Roses from their blood."
    new "Los ríos de Rosanna se volverán carmesí con rosas forjadas en su sangre."

    old "And I shall pay my wife's dowry until there are no more gifts to give."
    new "Y pagaré la dote de mi esposa hasta que no queden más regalos por dar."

    old "Sarah smiled as he left, knowing he spoke no idle words."
    new "Sarah sonrió al irse, sabiendo que no hablaba palabras vacías."

    old "As the gate to the warcamp opened, three great horses rode through."
    new "Mientras se abría la puerta del campamento de guerra, tres grandes caballos atravesaron el paso."

    old "Their manes black as ink, their skins brown like polished oak."
    new "Sus crines negras como tinta, sus pieles marrones como roble pulido."

    old "Atop them, three men, clearly Tribesmen judging by their complexion and ease with which they rode their horses."
    new "Encima de ellos, tres hombres, claramente tribales por su tez y la facilidad con la que montaban sus caballos."

    old "Hail, Sarah Rose."
    new "Salve, Sarah Rose."

    old "The man at the lead rode his horse ahead of the others."
    new "El hombre a la cabeza montaba su caballo por delante de los demás."

    old "We come bearing a message from Kamal, governor of Rosayi."
    new "Venimos con un mensaje de Kamal, gobernador de Rosayi."

    old "Rosayi. That is what the Tribesmen had renamed her land in her absence."
    new "Rosayi. Eso es lo que los Tribales habían renombrado a su tierra en su ausencia."

    old "I know of no such land, and no such governor."
    new "No conozco tal tierra ni tal gobernador."

    old "A king ruled these lands. Soon a queen."
    new "Un rey gobernaba estas tierras. Pronto, una reina."

    old "The Emmissary smiled."
    new "El Enviado sonrió."

    old "A Queen with no crown. A Queen with no throne. A Queen with no land."
    new "Una reina sin corona. Una reina sin trono. Una reina sin tierra."

    old "You are no more Queen of these lands than any other who claims it. Only the one who sits on the throne rules it."
    new "Eres reina de estas tierras tan poco como cualquiera que lo reclame; solo quien se sienta en el trono la gobierna."

    old "Worry not. That will be set right soon enough."
    new "No te preocupes. Pronto todo se pondrá bien."

    old "Governor Kamal, who rules in name of the Great Khan, Hassar, has extended to you a kindness."
    new "El Gobernador Kamal, quien gobierna en nombre del Gran Kan Hassar, te ha ofrecido un gesto de bondad."

    old "The Emmissary threw a rolled up scroll at her feet."
    new "El Emisario lanzó un pergamino enrollado a sus pies."

    old "It landed there, but Sarah did not bow down to pick it up."
    new "Cayó allí, pero Sarah no se inclinó para recogerla."

    old "Khan? My news tells me your Khan has died. That there are as many Khans as there are ambitious fools."
    new "¿Khan? Mis noticias me dicen que tu Khan ha muerto. Que hay tantos Khans como ambiciosos tontos."

    old "The Emmissary's face revealed a hint of discomfort. Perhaps he had not expected her to know of such things."
    new "El rostro del Emisario reveló una pizca de incomodidad. Quizás no había esperado que ella supiera de tales cosas."

    old "Rumors, spread by weaklings that cannot take by strength, so they try to take it by speaking lies."
    new "Rumores, propagados por débiles que no pueden tomar con fuerza, así que intentan hacerlo hablando mentiras."

    old "So your Khan still lives?"
    new "¿Tu Kan todavía vive?"

    old "The Emmissary gave no answer."
    new "El emisario no respondió."

    old "Tell me, what does your Kamal want?"
    new "Dime, ¿qué quiere tu Kamal?"

    old "He grants you and all your men, a pardon for your treason."
    new "Te concede a ti y a todos tus hombres un perdón por tu traición."

    old "Sarah almost had to laugh."
    new "Sarah casi tuvo que reír."

    old "A...pardon?"
    new "¿Eh... perdón?"

    old "Yes. He will forgive all of you for your attempts at usurping him rightful throne."
    new "Sí. Él perdonará a todos por sus intentos de usurpar su legítimo trono."

    old "He will allow all of you to breakdown your camp and return to the seas, back from where you came."
    new "Él os permitirá que rompáis vuestro campamento y vuelváis al mar, de donde venís."

    old "By vows spoken under a full moon, he swears."
    new "Por juramentos pronunciados bajo una luna llena, él lo jura."

    old "Kind offers, but whatever throne he sits on is not his by right, he stole it."
    new "Ofrece amabilidad, pero el trono en el que se sienta no es suyo por derecho; lo robó."

    old "He seized by force. By strength."
    new "Lo agarró con fuerza. Con poder."

    old "Such is the only right by which any ruler can make claim to anything."
    new "Tal es el único derecho por el cual cualquier gobernante puede reclamar algo."

    old "Have you come here to debate philosophies? Because I have not the appetite."
    new "¿Has venido aquí a debatir filosofías? Porque no tengo el apetito."

    old "Very well, then if Governor Kamal's kindness will not sway you, then let his threats do."
    new "Muy bien, pues si la bondad del gobernador Kamal no logra conmoverle, que sus amenazas lo hagan."

    old "His threats?"
    new "¿Sus amenazas?"

    old "Should you reject this kindness to withdraw, Governor Kamal promised that he would spare you nothing."
    new "Si rechazas esta bondad y te retiras, el gobernador Kamal prometió que no te perdonaría nada."

    old "He will send his armies out in full, to fight you on the plains of Rosanna, a land he knows well since the passing of these years."
    new "Él enviará a sus ejércitos completos para luchar contra ti en las llanuras de Rosanna, una tierra que conoce bien desde hace años."

    old "He will shatter your host, which is as weak as your brother's army was when he destroyed on the fields outside of your capital."
    new "Él romperá tu ejército, que es tan débil como el de tu hermano cuando destruyó los campos fuera de tu capital."

    old "He will kill every last man and woman that does not yield in battle."
    new "Matará a cada hombre y mujer que no se rinda en la batalla."

    old "He will bind in chains and shackles, those whose coward heart's cause them to surrender."
    new "Atará en cadenas y grilletes a aquellos cuyo corazón cobarde les induce a rendirse."

    old "And once he has broken you, he will drag you along at the head of a great slave caravan, back to Al'Gahaem."
    new "Y una vez que te haya roto, te arrastrará a la cabeza de una gran caravana de esclavos, de vuelta a Al'Gahaem."

    old "And he will make of you and your pitiful soldiers, the greatest gift to our Khan."
    new "Y de ti y de tus pobres soldados hará el mayor regalo para nuestro Kan."

    old "Every house of the Tribes will be spoiled for slaves, for generations."
    new "Cada casa de las Tribus será arruinada por esclavos, por generaciones."

    old "And you, Lady Rose, he will keep as a prized possession for his own delights."
    new "Y tú, Dama Rose, él te conservará como un tesoro preciado para sus propios deleites."

    old "Sarah felt the dread building in her chest as the man uttered his threats."
    new "Sarah sintió cómo el terror se acumulaba en su pecho mientras el hombre pronunciaba sus amenazas."

    old "Least of all, because she knew none of the words were spoken idly."
    new "Por último de todo, porque sabía que ninguna de las palabras había sido dicha en broma."

    old "If they lost this war...everything the man threatend would come to pass."
    new "Si perdían esta guerra... todo lo que el hombre amenazaba se cumpliría."

    old "Sarah drew in the cold air, steeling herself. She could not afford to show even a hint of fear."
    new "Sarah inhaló el aire frío, endureciéndose. No podía permitirse mostrar ni siquiera un atisbo de miedo."

    old "She was forged from the same iron as her father."
    new "Fue forjada del mismo hierro que su padre."

    old "Take your offer of kindness, and your threats. Words, that will be as lasting as your frail Khanate."
    new "Acepta tu oferta de bondad y tus amenazas. Palabras que durarán tanto como tu frágil Kanato."

    old "Return to your Governor and tell him my own promise."
    new "Vuelve a tu Gobernador y dile mi propia promesa."

    old "Tell him that I will drag him from the throne that he despoils by his mere presence."
    new "Dile que lo arrastraré del trono que profana con su mera presencia."

    old "Tell him that I will slit his fat throat from ear-to-ear, personally."
    new "Dile que lo cortaré personalmente, abriéndole el cuello gordo de oreja a oreja."

    old "Tell him that if he flees back to the desert that he crawled out of, I might consider letting him take a coward's refuge."
    new "Dile que si huye al desierto de donde salió arrastrando sus patas, podría considerar darle cobijo a un cobarde."

    old "But if he faces me in battle, I will spare not a soul."
    new "Pero si se enfrenta a mí en combate, no perdonaré ni una sola alma."

    old "Not of his armies, not of his household, not of his kin."
    new "No de sus ejércitos, no de su casa, no de su familia."

    old "Your people killed my brother, and each of you are guilty of that bloodsin."
    new "Su gente mató a mi hermano, y cada una de ustedes es culpable de esa sangre derramada."

    old "And each of you owes a debt for his life, that will be paid."
    new "Cada uno de ustedes debe pagar con su vida la deuda que tiene, y será cobrada."

    old "And tell him that I will stack up the bodies of your Tribesmen onto the scale of my brother's life, and I will still find the balance lacking."
    new "Y dile que apilaré los cadáveres de tus tribus sobre la balanza de la vida de mi hermano, y aun así faltará el equilibrio."

    old "Sarah rested her hands on the hilt of her blade."
    new "Sarah apoyó sus manos en el mango de su espada."

    old "In Rosanna, we take no slaves."
    new "En Rosanna no tomamos esclavos."

    old "Remember that when your army breaks and you throw yourself at my feet."
    new "Recuerda que cuando tu ejército se rompa y te arrojes a mis pies."

    old "The Emmissary's face remained stoic."
    new "El rostro del Emisario permaneció impasible."

    old "For a while, a heavy silence loomed."
    new "Durante un rato, se cernió un pesado silencio."

    old "I have delivered the message of Governor Kamal."
    new "Le he entregado el mensaje del Gobernador Kamal."

    old "And I have taken note of your response."
    new "Y he tomado nota de tu respuesta."

    old "I will deliver your message back to him."
    new "Entregaré tu mensaje de vuelta a él."

    old "The Emmissary kicked his heels into the sides of his horse, driving it into a gallop."
    new "El Emisario pateó los talones contra los flancos de su caballo, impulsándolo al galope."

    old "Ride!"
    new "¡Cabalgá!"

    old "Together, the three men turned and left, riding out of camp just as they came."
    new "Juntos, los tres hombres se giraron y se marcharon, saliendo del campamento apenas habían llegado."

    old "Sarah watched them until they passed across the horizon, black specks against the white snow."
    new "Sarah las observó hasta que cruzaron el horizonte, puntos negros contra la nieve blanca."

    old "The first threats of the war had been uttered."
    new "Ya habían sonado los primeros gritos de guerra."

    old "Now the bloodshed would follow."
    new "Ahora seguiría la carnicería."

    old "Sarah reached down and grabbed the letter."
    new "Sarah se agachó y tomó la carta."

    old "Holding it in her balled fist, she stomped through her camp back to her warroom."
    new "Sosteniéndolo en su puño cerrado, se abalanzó por su campamento de vuelta a su sala de guerra."

    old "Sarah was sitting behind her desk, the letter from Kamal rolled up."
    new "Sarah estaba sentada detrás de su escritorio, con la carta de Kamal enrollada."

    old "She had been staring at it for a while, working up the courage to read it."
    new "La había estado observando por un tiempo, acumulando la valentía necesaria para leerla."

    old "Finally, she just grabbed it and unscrolled the parchment."
    new "Finalmente, solo lo agarró y desenrolló el pergamino."

    old "Her eyes rushed across the page, taking all of it in."
    new "Sus ojos recorrieron la página, absorbiendo todo."

    old "A promise of safety if she retreated."
    new "Una promesa de seguridad si se retiraba."

    old "Threats of what would be done to her, her army, her people, if they lost."
    new "Amenazas de lo que le harían a ella, a su ejército y a su pueblo si perdían."

    old "Nothing she hadn't expected to be in the letter."
    new "Nada que no hubiera esperado encontrar en la carta."

    old "It was signed by Kamal himself personally, the many that occupied her ancestral home."
    new "Fue firmado personalmente por Kamal mismo, los muchos que ocupaban su residencia ancestral."

    old "The reports she had read showed that the Tribesmen were unstable."
    new "Los informes que había leído mostraban que los tribales eran inestables."

    old "That the death of their Khan had caused them to fall back to infighting."
    new "Que la muerte de su Kan les hubiera llevado a caer en una lucha interna."

    old "If their position was weak, Kamal gave no hint of it."
    new "Si su posición era débil, Kamal no dio ninguna señal de ello."

    old "Or perhaps that was the point, Sarah thought. Appear strong to hide that you are weak."
    new "O quizás ese era el punto, pensó Sarah. Aparecer fuerte para ocultar que eres débil."

    old "She sighed as she put the letter back down."
    new "Suspiró al devolver la carta."

    old "Always guessing...she wished she knew with certainty what to do for once."
    new "Siempre adivinando... deseaba saber con certeza qué hacer, por una vez."

    old "Sarah pulled up the map of Rosanna, along with all the annotations she had written on it, marks about ideas, strategies."
    new "Sarah arrancó el mapa de Rosanna junto con todas las anotaciones que había escrito en él, marcas sobre ideas y estrategias."

    old "Studying it, she ended up coming back to the same decision that had always been there."
    new "Al observarla, terminó por volver a la misma decisión que siempre había estado allí."

    old "March on the city of Calshure, straight ahead to the capital, or go around it through the Hinterlands."
    new "Marchar hacia la ciudad de Calshure, directamente hacia la capital, o rodearla pasando por las Tierras del Interior."

    old "Each had its own risks."
    new "Cada uno tenía sus propios riesgos."

    old "Calshure was a large city, and sieging it would be difficult. But if they took it quick, it would become the perfect base to attack further inland."
    new "Calshure era una gran ciudad, y asediarla sería difícil. Pero si la tomaban rápido, se convertiría en la base perfecta para atacar más hacia el interior."

    old "The Hinterlands were more open. Small towns and villages."
    new "Las Tierras de los Fondos eran más abiertas. Pequeños pueblos y aldeas."

    old "Those were the types of terrains that the Tribesmen liked to fight on. Open, spread out."
    new "Eran los tipos de terreno que a los tribales les gustaba pelear: abierto y despejado."

    old "But the heavy snowfall disfavored their cavlary army."
    new "Pero la intensa nevada desfavorecía a su ejército de caballería."

    old "And moving through the Hinterlands meant avoiding any long siege. She could march directly on the capital."
    new "Y cruzar las Tierras Profundas implicaba evitar cualquier sitio sitiado. Podía marchar directamente hacia la capital."

    old "Sarah traced each option with her fingers."
    new "Sarah trazó cada opción con los dedos."

    old "There was something to be said for each."
    new "Cada uno tenía algo que decir."

    old "But she could only make one decision."
    new "Pero solo pudo tomar una decisión."

    old "March on Calshure"
    new "Marcha sobre Calshure"

    old "Sarah tapped the map with her finger. It was decided."
    new "Sarah tocó el mapa con su dedo. Había tomado la decisión."

    old "She would march on the city of Calshure."
    new "Marcharía sobre la ciudad de Calshure."

    old "March through the Hinterlands"
    new "Marchar por los Hinterlands"

    old "She would march her army through the Hinterlands."
    new "Marcharía su ejército a través de las Tierras Profundas."
